      "writtenOn": "2025-09-06T03:12:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment is a bit confusing. It seems to contradict [docs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/ns-d3d12-d3d12_feature_data_architecture):\n\u003e [on non-CC UMA], a single residency budget is available but the UMA design commonly benefits from the three heap attributions.\n\u003e ... some UMA adapters benefit from both the no-CPU-access and write-combine properties of default and upload heaps.\n\nBut in practice the result of the outer logic is that we\u0027re saying \"on UMA, all heaps are GPU-queue-accessible\". I think it would be clearer if instead of a `D3D12_HEAP_TYPE` we returned our own `enum class { Readback, Upload, GPUQueueAccessible }`.\n\nWith the caveat that I don\u0027t think \"GPU-queue-accessible\" necessarily means \"fast to access\".",
      "revId": "7627b30e242dca61e2f600a7fd29085601d771fc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
